repository-code: "https://github.com/sparkainlp-x/oes32-membrane-array"
url: "https://sparkainlpx.xyz"
abstract: >-
  OES32 Membrane Array is a small Python companion to oes32-membrane-shield.
  It composes the fixed 32-slot OES32 membrane contract into arrays of 32 to
  65,536 channel slots, always as a whole number of independent 32-slot cells,
  without changing the upstream API. One external Ed25519 capability
  authorizes the whole flattened frame and binds the channel count. Every cell
  is validated before any state changes, so an update is accepted or rejected
  as one transaction; a residual breach latches an array-wide breaker that
  needs a guardian reset. Calibration requires independent CALIBRATEUR and
  GARDIEN approvals, and symmetry rules apply within each cell. Scope: a
  software state-machine prototype on generated numbers. It is not a physical
  membrane, sensor array, hardware implementation, field result, medical
  device or performance benchmark; slot counts are configuration counts only,
  and no latency, throughput or independent security review is claimed.
